# C# Backend

## Active projects

| Project | Role |
|---------|------|
| `Asher.Core` | Models (`ManagedModInfo`, `AsherSettings`, `AsherPaths`), no UI deps |
| `Asher.Services` | Business logic implementations + `IAsherApplication` contract |
| `Asher.Host` | JSONL transport, `JsonlHostSession`, spawned by Electron |
| `Asher.Host.TestClient` | Protocol validation tool |
| `Asher.SDK` | Patching API for mod DLLs |
| `Asher.Launcher` | Game executable replacement; loads runtime |
| `Asher.Runtime` | In-game Harmony bootstrap |
| `Asher.Patching.*` | Individual mod assemblies (5 canonical mods) |

## Rules

- New Electron features should be exposed through `IAsherApplication` + JSONL, not ad-hoc IPC.
- Keep contracts DTO-oriented (`Asher.Services/Application/Contracts/`). Do not expose internal service types.
- Preserve existing service behavior unless a requirement explicitly demands a change.
- Do not introduce Electron, WPF, or Prism references in backend projects.
- Launcher and Runtime run inside the game process — keep them independent of Host.
- All `Asher.Host` stdout is JSONL protocol traffic. Use stderr for diagnostics.
- Build command: `dotnet build <project>.csproj -c Debug -p:Platform=x86`
- Do not modify unrelated projects merely for cleanup preferences.
